5. WHAT BANDWIDTH DOES THE TASK NEED? FEEDBACK-ONLY vs FEEDFORWARD + FEEDBACK
   Feedback-only: a circular turn of radius Rc at speed v is a reference at
   omega = v/Rc with amplitude Rc; for L = wc/s the tracking error is
   e = |S(j omega)| Rc = Rc omega/sqrt(omega^2+wc^2) -> v/wc for omega << wc.
   Feedforward (differential flatness, [D-01]): the reference is supplied open loop and
   the loop only rejects the model-error disturbance a_d, giving e ~ a_d/wc^2.
